# C# file headers and formatting

## Mandatory StyleCop file header

Every `.cs` file must start with the StyleCop header defined in `stylecop.json` (`xmlHeader: false`). Do **not** re-suppress `SA1633` in `.editorconfig`.

Canonical shape (affiliation comes from `{companyName}` → `NTU "KhPI"`):

```csharp
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// University: NTU "KhPI"
// Authors:
//   Yaroslav Kravets <beeengine1983@gmail.com>
//   ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3893-1607
//   Iryna Liutenko <cherliv68@gmail.com>
//   ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4357-1826
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

- Use **Western** name order (`Yaroslav Kravets`, `Iryna Liutenko`) in headers, `stylecop.json`, and assembly copyright attributes.
- Keep `copyrightText` using `University: {companyName}` so the affiliation is defined once in `companyName`.
- New or renamed `.cs` files must include this exact header (including under `src/HtmlScrapper/` when that project is explicitly in scope for the task).
- Wire `stylecop.json` via `Directory.Build.props` `AdditionalFiles`; do not remove that link.

## Formatting

Follow `.editorconfig` for this solution:

- UTF-8, LF, final newline, trim trailing whitespace
- 4-space indent for C#; 2-space for `*.{csproj,props,targets}`
- `this.` qualification for instance members (`IDE0009` / `dotnet_style_qualification_*`)
- Sorted usings (`dotnet_sort_system_directives_first`); remove unused usings (`IDE0005`)
- Prefer fixing via `dotnet build` / `dotnet format` warnings (`IDE0055`, StyleCop) over ad-hoc style changes

When adding code, match neighboring file style; do not mass-reformat unrelated files.
